module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.AlgebraizationCoherentFormal.GeneratorShifts
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Sequence.QuasiRegular.Basic

/-!
# Stacks 0EJS: algebraization of a coherent formal module along a regular sequence

Fix an algebraization situation (Stacks 0EHC): a Noetherian ring `A` with ideals `I ⊆ 𝔞`,
`X = Spec(A)`, `Y = V(I)`, `Z = V(𝔞)` and `U = X \ Z`. Let `(F_n)` be an object of
`Coh(U, I 𝒪_U)`. Stacks 0EJS assumes

1. there are `f₁, …, f_d ∈ I` such that for every `y ∈ U ∩ Y` the ideal `I 𝒪_{X,y}` is
   generated by `f₁, …, f_d` and `f₁, …, f_d` is an `F_y^∧`-regular sequence,
2. `H⁰(U, F_1)` and `H¹(U, F_1)` are finite `A`-modules,

and concludes that `(F_n)` extends canonically to `X`, and that `(F_n)` is the completion of a
coherent `𝒪_U`-module when `A` is complete.

The source's proof verifies the three conditions of Stacks 0EHH from the decomposition
`Iⁿ F_(n+1) = ⨁_{e₁ + ⋯ + e_d = n} F_1 · f₁^{e₁} ⋯ f_d^{e_d}`, checked on stalks by
quasi-regularity of the `fᵢ` on `F_y^∧` (Algebra 00LN). This file proves that decomposition and
feeds it to `Stacks.Algebraization.canonicallyExtends_of_idealPowerDesc`, which carries out the
rest of the argument (Cohomology 0GYK and 0GYM) for any finite family of elements of `I`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.QuasiregularSequence.coeff_mem_of_isRegular_ofFn` and
  `Stacks.QuasiregularSequence.exists_eq_sum_monomial_smul` — quasi-regularity of a regular
  sequence and the monomial description of `Jⁿ M`, indexed by `Fin d`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.bijective_stalk_idealPowerDesc_of_completedStalk` — the stalk maps of
  `Stacks.Algebraization.idealPowerDesc` are bijective as soon as, on every formal stalk along
  `U ∩ Y`, the components give an injection and a surjection modulo the next power of `I`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.exists_isIso_idealPowerDesc_of_regularSequence` — the decomposition of
  `Iⁿ⁺¹ F_(n+2)` into copies of `F_1` indexed by the monomials of degree `n + 1` in the `fᵢ`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.canonicallyExtends_of_regularSequence` — **Stacks 0EJS**.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.essImage_completionFunctor_of_regularSequence` — its second sentence.

## Implementation notes

Hypothesis (1) is `Stacks.Algebraization.HasRegularSequenceOnCompletedStalks` and hypothesis (2)
is `Stacks.Algebraization.HasFiniteLowDegreeCohomology`. The terms of `(F_n)` are indexed from
zero, so the source's `F_1` is the term of index `0`.

The `fᵢ` are not assumed to generate `I`, only `I 𝒪_{X,y}` along `U ∩ Y`; off `U ∩ Y` every
stalk of every `F_n` vanishes, so the decomposition is still an isomorphism there.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EJS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EJS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EHH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EHH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00LN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00LN)
-/

